.TH BENCH 1
.SH NAME
bench \- measure the disk path from a program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bench
.RI [ mib ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bench
measures the way a file request travels: program, file server, disk
driver, disk, every step a message. It writes
.I mib
MiB (default 16) to
.B /tmp/bench.dat
in requests of 128 KiB and commits it, reads it back, then creates 500
small files, looks one up, and deletes them. Each line gives a rate and
the time it took.
.SH FILES
.B /tmp/bench.dat
and
.BR /tmp/b. *
(removed at the end).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fs (4),
.BR vblk (4),
.BR df (1)
